 {:seon.task/name "a-commit-of-no-text-starts-no-round"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by Optimization (2026-11-10, building main's content mark, docs/storage.md#mains-content-mark). seon.vector/vectors-proc runs a round at every main commit notice (seon.vector/round: the commit's db made, one datoms-diff since the last round's commit, due's seeks), though nearly every commit is records (an agent's status per request) or its own embedding write, which hold no text. The notice already carries the commit's resolved datoms (:ops), as the test service and the fork server read them (seon.program/moves-program?). Cut: a notice whose :ops hold no datom of a text attribute (seon.vector/texts), with nothing owed and the proc caught up, starts no round; the next round's diff from the last commit it scanned still finds every text since. The proc's tests build notices without :ops (vector-test's note): they must carry the commit's ops, as the writer's do. Estimate first: what a round costs on a records-only commit on a 2,931-form main (n = the datoms since the last round; expected the diff and an at-commit, under 1 ms), and how often it runs (every request). Proof: seon.vector-test/a-commit-of-no-text-starts-no-round (a status-only notice: no round, no read; a form's notice: a round)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-test/a-commit-of-no-text-starts-no-round}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-cold-near-costs-its-shortlist-not-its-leaves"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by context (2026-11-15 ~09:05, landing 4's estimate, root's REPL on main). [M] seon.vector/near over the forms (:of :form/id, 6,354 rows, shortlist 400) cold: 47M ticks / 327 MB; the same call again at once: 5.2M / 31 MB; once 170M / 1.8 GB (result/a0b2ca5d, result/ccd89b79). The rows are kept (rows-of: 119 ticks a hit) and fine-scores over 400 warm costs 4.1M / 20 MB, so the gap is the cold reads of the shortlist's :seon.vector/f16 values (1,536 bytes each, over :seon.config.store/value-out-of-line-bytes), each seek loading and decoding a leaf node (H: zstd node + out-of-line fetch per value). Lower bound: 400 x 1.5 KB = 0.6 MB read; 10x over is ~6 MB. Find where the bytes go (seon.profile/measure! with the store's node cache cold), then fix at the storage cause (keep the f16 rows beside the coarse rows as rows-of keeps those, or read them in entity order so one leaf serves many). seon.ctx.search/relevance pays this every cold call (119M-190M ticks whole)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-cost-test/a-cold-near-costs-its-shortlist}}]
